  "title": "The community project garden grew",
  "summary": "June made Pollinations easier to discover and more capable to build with, expanding the community project garden while sharpening image and text infrastructure.\n\nThe directory gained a broad crop of community-built tools, games, bots, creative experiments, and Vibe Coding projects, with clearer documentation and listings that make the ecosystem easier to explore.\n\nDeepSeek R1-0528, ElixpoSearch, o3, and gpt-4o-mini-search-preview expanded the text lineup; o3 gained image input, while cleaner availability data and tier metadata made the growing catalog easier for apps to navigate.\n\nGPT Image gained transparent-background output for assets that can go straight into compositions, alongside better repeat-request caching, safer image handling, overlay branding, and an early semantic cache experiment.\n\nDefault text traffic moved to openai-fast, streaming and routing were cleaned up, account-specific model mapping laid groundwork for personalized choices, and performance tracking made the text stack easier to inspect in the wild.",
